1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,914
This is the Runwal Enterprises I P O, a mainboard offer,

2
00:00:03,914 --> 00:00:08,107
open from the twenty-fifth to the twenty-ninth of September.

3
00:00:08,607 --> 00:00:11,527
The price band is ₹290 to ₹305.

4
00:00:11,527 --> 00:00:17,273
Every figure here comes from the final red herring prospectus

5
00:00:17,273 --> 00:00:19,251
and exchange notices;

6
00:00:19,251 --> 00:00:22,924
the final price is fixed after bidding,

7
00:00:22,924 --> 00:00:26,975
so valuations are computed at the ₹305 cap.

8
00:00:27,475 --> 00:00:28,712
First, the business.

9
00:00:29,212 --> 00:00:33,005
Runwal is a Mumbai residential real-estate developer,

10
00:00:33,005 --> 00:00:36,368
known for large townships that include schools,

11
00:00:36,368 --> 00:00:38,300
malls and shopping arcades.

12
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:43,463
Real-estate revenue is lumpy:

13
00:00:43,463 --> 00:00:50,377
₹2,408.87 Cr in FY24, ₹1,007.77 Cr in FY25,

14
00:00:50,377 --> 00:00:54,397
and ₹1,798.95 Cr in FY26,

15
00:00:54,397 --> 00:01:02,437
because sales are recognised as projects complete.

16
00:01:02,937 --> 00:01:04,537
The financial checkpoint.

17
00:01:05,037 --> 00:01:17,416
FY26 revenue was ₹1,798.95 Cr, against ₹1,007.77 Cr in FY25,

18
00:01:17,416 --> 00:01:21,336
a change of 78.51%.

19
00:01:21,836 --> 00:01:29,900
Profit after tax was ₹185.76 Cr, a margin of 10.33%.

20
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:32,384
The balance sheet is the key lens.

21
00:01:32,884 --> 00:01:38,912
Net debt was ₹2,778.11 Cr at March 2026,

22
00:01:38,912 --> 00:01:44,187
against total equity of ₹844.82 Cr,

23
00:01:44,187 --> 00:01:49,311
so net debt is about 3.29x equity.

24
00:01:49,811 --> 00:01:53,683
The offer size at the cap is ₹500.00 Cr,

25
00:01:53,683 --> 00:01:56,296
and it is 100% fresh issue.

26
00:01:56,796 --> 00:01:59,181
All of that money goes into the company;

27
00:01:59,181 --> 00:02:02,044
no existing shareholder is selling in this deal.

28
00:02:02,544 --> 00:02:03,867
Where does the money go?

29
00:02:04,367 --> 00:02:07,231
The whole ₹500.00 Cr is fresh money;

30
00:02:07,231 --> 00:02:09,380
there is no offer for sale.

31
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:13,645
₹100.00 Cr repays the company's own debt,

32
00:02:13,645 --> 00:02:17,502
and ₹225.00 Cr goes into two subsidiaries,

33
00:02:17,502 --> 00:02:22,552
Evie Real Estate and Runwal Residency, to repay theirs.

34
00:02:23,052 --> 00:02:28,193
The balance can fund future project acquisitions and general corporate purposes.

35
00:02:28,693 --> 00:02:29,696
Valuation.

36
00:02:30,196 --> 00:02:32,716
At the ₹305 cap,

37
00:02:32,716 --> 00:02:40,905
the price is 18.22x FY26 earnings of ₹16.74 a share.

38
00:02:41,405 --> 00:02:46,708
That is below all its listed peers:

39
00:02:46,708 --> 00:02:55,648
Sunteck at 21.09x, Oberoi 25.88x, Godrej Properties 27.53x,

40
00:02:55,648 --> 00:03:00,648
Lodha 33.42x and Prestige 51.70x.

41
00:03:01,148 --> 00:03:05,841
The discount partly reflects much higher leverage and lumpy profits.

42
00:03:06,341 --> 00:03:07,835
Now balance the evidence.

43
00:03:08,335 --> 00:03:09,559
Watch-out:

44
00:03:09,559 --> 00:03:12,375
Net debt ~3.29x equity.

45
00:03:12,375 --> 00:03:13,477
Strength:

46
00:03:13,477 --> 00:03:14,824
100% fresh:

47
00:03:14,824 --> 00:03:17,273
no promoter selling.

48
00:03:17,773 --> 00:03:19,538
Watch-out:

49
00:03:19,538 --> 00:03:22,008
Lumpy revenue:

50
00:03:22,008 --> 00:03:26,595
FY25 fell to ₹1,007.77 Cr.

51
00:03:26,595 --> 00:03:28,183
Strength:

52
00:03:28,183 --> 00:03:32,771
FY26 PAT up to ₹185.76 Cr.

53
00:03:33,271 --> 00:03:34,480
Watch-out:

54
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:39,319
₹325.00 Cr of proceeds only repays debt.

55
00:03:39,319 --> 00:03:40,407
Strength:

56
00:03:40,407 --> 00:03:45,004
18.22x P/E, below listed Mumbai peers.

57
00:03:45,504 --> 00:03:46,635
How to apply.

58
00:03:47,135 --> 00:03:51,652
The minimum bid is one lot of 49 shares,

59
00:03:51,652 --> 00:03:54,815
which is ₹14,945 at the cap.

60
00:03:55,315 --> 00:03:58,790
Retail investors can bid up to two lakh rupees,

61
00:03:58,790 --> 00:04:02,931
and allotment is by lottery if retail is oversubscribed.

62
00:04:03,431 --> 00:04:07,974
Check live subscription on the N S E or B S E website,

63
00:04:07,974 --> 00:04:09,404
not social media.

64
00:04:09,904 --> 00:04:10,864
Let's recap.

65
00:04:11,364 --> 00:04:18,554
FY26 revenue ₹1,798.95 Cr, profit ₹185.76 Cr.

66
00:04:18,554 --> 00:04:22,389
The offer is 100% fresh.

67
00:04:22,389 --> 00:04:28,780
Valuation is 18.22x earnings at the cap.

68
00:04:28,780 --> 00:04:34,212
The minimum investment is ₹14,945.

69
00:04:34,712 --> 00:04:38,886
This video is public-source education from the red herring

70
00:04:38,886 --> 00:04:41,188
prospectus and exchange notices.

71
00:04:41,188 --> 00:04:45,146
It is not investment advice and not a buy or sell call.

72
00:04:45,146 --> 00:04:46,945
Read the final documents,

73
00:04:46,945 --> 00:04:49,824
check live subscription on the exchange,

74
00:04:49,824 --> 00:04:52,558
and consult a SEBI-registered adviser.

75
00:04:52,558 --> 00:04:53,997
Thanks for watching.

